<section id="mission" class="report-container pb-16 md:pb-20">
  <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-[1.2fr_0.8fr] md:items-start">
    <div><p class="mb-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-brand-text">The problem</p><h2 class="text-3xl text-ink md:text-4xl">A sedentary day is not a personal failure. It is a product problem.</h2><div class="prose prose-site mt-6 max-w-[65ch] prose-p:leading-8"><p>In 2022, 31% of adults worldwide — approximately 1.8 billion people — did not meet the World Health Organization’s recommended levels of physical activity. WHO recommends limiting sedentary time and says that replacing it with movement of any intensity brings health benefits.</p><p>A height-adjustable desk already has the mechanical capability. What it usually lacks is a calm, useful feedback loop that helps a person notice the moment and choose to change position.</p></div><p class="mt-5 text-xs leading-5 text-ink-muted">Sources: <a class="report-link" href="https://www.who.int/news/item/26-06-2024-nearly-1.8-billion-adults-at-risk-of-disease-from-not-doing-enough-physical-activity" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">WHO activity report</a> and <a class="report-link" href="https://www.who.int/publications/i/item/9789240015128" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">WHO guidelines</a>.</p></div>
    <aside class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-6"><p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-muted">One global signal</p><div class="mt-3 text-5xl font-semibold text-brand-text">31%</div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-ink-muted">of adults were not meeting recommended activity levels in 2022.</p><div class="mt-6 border-t border-line pt-5"><p class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">1.8 billion</p><p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-ink-muted">people represented by that estimate.</p></div></aside>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-12 max-w-3xl border-l-2 border-brand-strong/50 pl-5"><p class="text-xl leading-8 text-ink">If I can address a problem that affects millions of people with the tools I know, I can build products that are more universal, more ergonomic, and genuinely useful. Open Smart Desk is one of those attempts.</p><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-6 text-ink-muted">The goal is not to control a person or make a medical claim. It is to combine ergonomics, user experience and local, multiplatform software into a tool that supports a better everyday habit.</p></div>
</section>
